meta {
  name: Generate Upload URL
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/signed-upload-url
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "files": [
      {
        "fileName": "profile-pic.jpg",
        "contentType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    ],
    "folder": "avatars"
  }
}

docs {
  ## Generate Signed Upload URL

  Accepts an array of file descriptors and returns pre-signed PutObject URLs (30-min expiry)
  so the client can upload files directly to Cloudflare R2.

  ### Request Body
  | Field    | Type   | Required | Description                                    |
  |----------|--------|----------|------------------------------------------------|
  | files    | array  | ✅       | Array of `{ fileName, contentType }` objects   |
  | folder   | string | No       | Subfolder within user's directory              |

  ### Headers
  | Header        | Value               | Required |
  |---------------|---------------------|----------|
  | Authorization | Bearer {{authToken}}| ✅       |

  ### Success Response (200)
  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "data": [
      {
        "key": "uuid/profile-pic.jpg",
        "signedUrl": "https://...",
        "publicUrl": "https://..."
      }
    ]
  }
  ```

  ### Error Responses
  - **400** — Invalid file entries
  - **401** — Missing/invalid token
}
